{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>When YHWH your Elohim cuts off the nations.</b> This passage warns a person not to serve the Holy One, blessed be He, with the service of idolatry. And He gave a reason for this: ״כל תועבת ה׳ אשר שנא עשו לאלהיהם״ — every abomination of YHWH which He hates, they did for their elohim. And it says: ״ופן תדרוש לאלהיהם לאמר איכה יעבדו הגוים האלה את אלהיהם ואעשה כן גם אני״ — lest you inquire of their elohim, saying, How do these nations serve their elohim, and I will do likewise for the Holy One, blessed be He — doing for Him what they do for the idol — and you think this is a good path and the Holy One, blessed be He, desires it. ״לא תעשה כן״ — you shall not do so. Why? ״כי כל תועבת ה׳ אשר שנא עשו לאלהיהם״ — for every abomination of YHWH which He hates, they did for their elohim. That is to say: they go seeking after the things that the Holy One, blessed be He, hates, and they do them. And as it is written concerning the wicked who deny Him (Psalms 36:3): ״כי החליק אליו בעיניו למצוא עונו לשנוא״ — for he flatters himself in his own eyes, to find his iniquity to hate — that is, they signal with their eyes and look to find a transgression that the Holy One, blessed be He, hates, and they commit it. So too it says here concerning these nations: they found no abomination more grievous before the Holy One, blessed be He, than the burning of children, and behold, they do so. And this is what it says: ״כי גם את בניהם ואת בנותיהם ישרפו באש לאלהיהם״ — for even their sons and their daughters they burn in fire to their elohim — that is, even man, who is the choicest of all species, for whom alone the Holy One, blessed be He, created His world — behold, they burn them in fire to their elohim. And it says: ״את כל הדבר אשר אנכי מצוה אתכם״ — all the matter that I command you — this is the matter of the offerings and the Temple service; and it comes to teach that He hates the one and chooses the other." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״כי יכרית ה׳ אלהיך את הגוים״ — To what may the matter be compared? To a king who planted a vineyard in his field, and within it were great cedars and thorns. The king went and cut down the cedars and left the thorns. His servants said to him: Our lord the king — the thorns that used to snag our garments and tear them, you left; and the cedars you cut down? He said to them: Had I cut down the thorns and left the cedars, with what would I fence my vineyard? And I would not have done well. Rather, let the vineyard stand as it is, and I will kindle a fire among them. So too Israel is the vineyard of the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is said (Isaiah 5:7): ״כי כרם ה׳ צבאות בית ישראל״. He brought Israel into the land and cut down the cedars that were in it, as it is said (Amos 2:9): ״ואנכי השמדתי את האמורי מפניכם אשר כגובה ארזים גבהו וחסון הוא כאלונים״, and He left their children and their children's children there, in order that they might guard the vineyard, as it is said (Judges 3:1): ״ואלה הגוים אשר הניח ה׳ לנסות בם את ישראל״, and it is written (Judges 3:2): ״למען נסות בם את ישראל השומרים הם את דרך ה׳ ללכת בם״. And when the vineyard stands as it is, in the watch of the Torah (Isaiah 33:12): ״והיו עמים משרפות שיד קוצים כסוחים באש יצתו״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:07.627087401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}